\par
\par
KEY TO FIMICOLOUS DISCOMYCETES\par
\par
\par
\b 1) \b0 Asci more or less cylindric, usually non-protruding at maturity above the general level of  the hymenium, \par
     with a functional operculum. Spores uniseriate, exceptionally biseriate or irregularly arranged. Ascomata\par
     comparatively large (with rare exceptions), usually discoidal or cup-shaped, rarely pulvinate.    \b 2\b0\par
\b 1*) \b0 Asci cylindric-claviform or clavate up to saccate or subglobose, exceptionally cylindric, protruding at maturity,\par
       operculate or inoperculate. Spores biseriate to conglobate, rarely uniseriate. Ascomata usually minute, pulvinate\par
       to subglobose, with several intermediate forms, exceptionally discoidal.   \b 26\par
\b0\par
\b 2) \b0 Asci amyloid (with a few exceptions). Paraphyses not containing carotenoid pigments. Receptacle margins\par
     glabrous. Hymenial surface (disc) never bright orange or red (\b\i Pezizaceae \b0\i0 Dumort.). Ascomata cup-shaped,\par
     in the early stages at least, sessile or rarely (sub)stipitate, almost always and at least partly with brown shades,\par
     often > 10 mm diam. \i Excipulum\b  \b0\i0 not embedded in a gelatinous material. (\b\i Peziza\b0\i0 )           \b 3\b0                                 \b\par
2*)\b0  Asci non-amyloid. Paraphyses with or without carotenoid pigments. Margin of the receptacles usually hairy or\par
      setulose. Disc sometimes brightly coloured. \lang1040 Ascomata rarely > 10 mm diam. \b   \b0 (\b\i Pyronemataceae \b0\i0 Corda, \b\i p.p.\b0\i0 )\b\i           \lang2057\i0 6\b0\par
\par
\b 3) \b0 Spores smooth.   \b 4\par
3*) \b0 Spores finely warted. \b 5\par
\par
4)\b0  Ascomata deeply cupulate, up to 150 mm diam. Disc pale ochreous-yellowish, vesiculose due to the loosening \par
     hymenium. \i Excipulum\i0  5-layered, with a middle medullary layer of a \i textura intricata\i0 . Spores 20-21.6 x 11.2-\par
     12.6 \'b5m (20-24 x 10-14 \'b5m, \cf1 Hohmeyer\cf0 , 1986). $ \b\i Peziza vesiculosa\par
\i0 4*) \b0 Ascomata comparatively small (up to 20 mm diam.), shallow-cupulate but tending to flatten. Disc darker,\par
       brownish, more or less regular (not loosening from the underlying flesh). \i Excipulum\b  \b0\i0 3-layered (\i textura \b\i0\par
       \b0\i globulosa\i0 ). Spores 20-22.5  x 10-11.7 \'b5m (19-22 x 9.5-12, \cf1 Hohmeyer\cf0 , 1986). $ \b\i Peziza fimeti\par
\par
\i0 5) \b0 Ascomata sessile. Spores 17.1-18 x 8.5-9 \'b5m (15-18 x 7-8.5, \cf1 Hohmeyer\cf0 , 1986). On human dung.\par
                                  $\b  \i Peziza merdae\b0\i0                                                                                                       \par
\b 5*) \b0 Ascomata sessile or more often stipitate. Spores 14.1-15.7 x 6.8-7.8 \'b5m (13-16.5 x 6.5-7.5, \cf1 Hohmeyer\cf0 , 1986).  \par
      On herbivore dung. $ \b\i Peziza perdicina\b0\i0\par
\par
\b 6) \b0 Ascomata (apothecia) sessile, discoidal or pulvinate at maturity, rarely shallow cupulate or turbinate. Hymenial \par
     surface brightly coloured with several yellow, orange and red shades.  Paraphyses containing carotenoid \par
     pigments. Hairs (setulae) usually deeply rooting. \b 7\i\par
\i0 6*) \b0 Ascomata often cupulate or scutellate, sessile or short stipitate. Disc not brightly coloured, white, greyish,\par
       purple-brown, yellowish. Paraphyses lacking carotenoid pigments. Hairs usually superficial. \b 18\b0\par
\par
\b 7) \b0 Spores guttulate, hyaline, lacking a refractive yellowish pigment in lactic cotton blue. Perisporium usually\par
     non-loosening, even less separable, by such a staining (\b\i Scutellinia\b0\i0 ). Spores 17.8-21 x 11.5-13.6 \'b5m.\par
     Hairs dark brown, often more than 1000 \'b5m long. $ \b\i Scutellinia crinita\par
\i0 7*) \b0 Spores eguttulate, containing a refractive yellowish pigment. Perisporium easily loosening as well as separable \par
      and floating in lactic cotton blue. Hairs usually paler and less than 1000 \'b5m long. (\b\i Cheilymenia\b0\i0 )           \b 8\b0\par
\par
\b 8) \b0 Hairs often not observable to the unaided eye, hyaline, pale yellowish or rarely yellowish-pale brown, superficial   \par
     to subrooting, thin-walled (usually < 2 \'b5m diam.). Medullary \i excipulum \i0 not or scarcely differentiated (\i textura\i0  \par
     \i globulosa-angularis\i0  or \i subintricata\i0 ) from the ectal \i excipulum\i0 , exceptionally differentiated (\i textura intricata\i0 ). \b 9\par
8*) \b0 Hairs observable to the unaided eye, dark yellow to yellowish-brown or dark reddish-brown, rooting,\par
      comparatively thick-walled (often > 2 \'b5m diam.). Medullary \i excipulum \i0 usually differentiated.  \b 13\par
\par
9) \b0 Ascomata minute (usually < 1 mm diam.), lasioboloid, turbinate or barrel-shaped. Marginal hairs superficial,\par
     rather dense, with a simple base, lying on an excipular abortive cell. Spores (sub)smooth. Medullary\par
     \i excipulum\b  \b0\i0  non- or hardly differentiated from the ectal one (\i textura globulosa-angularis\i0 ).   \b 10\par
9*) \b0 Ascomata larger (1.5-20 mm diam.), differently shaped. Marginal hairs superficial to subrooting, sometimes\par
       absent, not lying on an abortive cell. Spores ornamented with longitudinal cyanophilous striae, which \par
       sometimes anastomose and build up an incomplete reticulum.  \b 11\b0   \par
\par
\pard\tx284\tx426\tx851\b 10) \b0 Disc bright yellow-orange. Spores 21-24.5 x 12-13.5 \'b5m (18-25.5 x 12-14.5, \cf1 Moravec\cf0 , 1992).\par
\b\i                \b0\i0 $\lang1040  \b\i Cheilymenia pulcherrima \b0\i0  \par
\b 10*) \b0 Disc orange to reddish-orange. Spores 19-21.5 x 11-12.5 \'b5m (15-20 x 9-12, \cf1 Thind & Kaushal\cf0 , 1980).  \par
\pard         $ \b\i Cheilymenia aurantiacorubra\i0\par
\par
\b0  \lang2057\b 11) \b0 Ascomata medium-sized (up to 5 mm, rarely < 1.5 mm diam.), discoidal or shallow cupulate. Disc orange-\par
       yellow. Receptacles finely granulose, almost glabrous, with only sparse hyphoid hairs, particularly \par
       arranged at the base. Medullary \i excipulum\b  \b0\i0 of a \i textura globulosa\i0 -\i angularis\i0 , undifferentiated from the \par
       ectal \i excipulum\i0 . Spores 16-18 x 8-9 \'b5m. Paraphyses strongly inflated at the apices (up to 15 \'b5m diam.). \par
\pard\tx284\tx426\tx851                    $ \b\i Cheilymenia granulata\par
\i0 11*) \b0 Ascomata\b  \b0 medium-large (up to 20 mm diam.), discoidal to irregularly expanded (margin wavy, even lobate).\par
         Disc sulphur to egg yellow. Receptacles not granulose, apparently glabrous to hairy. Hairs differentiated, \par
         associated or not with hyphoid hairs. Medullary \i excipulum\b  \b0\i0 more differentiated. Paraphyses hardly inflated\par
\pard          at the apex.  \b 12\par
\par
\pard\tx284\tx426\tx851 12) \b0 Ascomata medium-sized, usually < 5 mm diam. Receptacles glabrous to the unaided eye. Marginal hairs very pale \par
      or hyaline, superficial (base bulbous or bulbous-lobate). Medullary \i excipulum\b  \b0\i0 not clearly differentiated, of a \par
      \i textura subintricata\i0  at most. Spores 16-20 x 7-10 \'b5m (16-19.5 x 8.5-10.5, \cf1 Yao & Spooner\cf0 , 1996a).\par
\pard       Usually fimicolous. $ \b\i Cheilymenia theleboloides\par
\pard\tx284\tx426\tx851\i0 12*) \b0 Ascomata comparatively large (often > 10 mm diam.), with marginal hairs sometimes observable even to the\par
         unaided eye, up to 1000 x 30 \'b5m, pale yellowish-brown, subrooting, multifurcate at the base. Medullary\b\i  \par
         \b0 excipulum\b  \b0\i0 of a \i textura subintricata\i0  or \i intricata\i0 .\b  \b0 Spores 14-18 x 7-10.5 \'b5m. Terricolous or muscicolous. \par
                      $ \b\i Cheilymenia vitellina\par
\pard\par
\pard\tx284\tx426\tx851\i0 13) \b0 Marginal setulae with a multifurcate base, made up of simple roots and short, coralloid or uncinate roots.\par
      Lateral asterosetulae (stellate, multicuspidate hairs) present. Ascomata shallow-cupulate or scutellate or even\par
      discoidal, with a marginal collarette. Disc more or less orange, lacking reddish shades. Spores almost smooth,\par
      15.3-17.1 x 8.1-8.5 \'b5m (14-18 x 8-10, \cf1 Denison\cf0 , 1964).   $ \b\i Cheilymenia stercorea \b0\i0 f. \b\i stercorea\par
\i0 13*) \b0 Marginal setulae with simple roots only. Lateral asterosetulae absent. Receptacles with or without a  marginal\par
         \lang1040 collarette. \b 14\par
\par
14) \b0 Ascomata barrel-shaped. Marginal collarette present. \lang2057 Disc yellow-orange. Medullary \i excipulum\b  \b0\i0 of a \i textura\i0  \par
\b\i       \b0\i0 (\i angularis\i0 )\b\i  \b0\i0 or \i subintricata\i0 . Marginal setulae furcate at the base but with short (truncate) roots. Asterosetulae\par
      absent  but sometimes replaced with hairs bifurcate at the apex. Spores ellipsoidal, 21-23 x 11-13 \'b5m (22-30 x \par
      10.5-16.5, \cf1 Moravec\cf0 , 1993). $ \b\i Cheilymenia insignis \b0\i0  \par
\b 14*) \b0 Ascomata usually more expanded. Marginal collarette absent but receptacles sometimes with a brownish margin.\par
         Medullary \i excipulum\i0  of a \i textura intricata\i0 . Marginal setulae with longer root(s). Bifurcate superficial hairs \par
\pard          absent. \b 15\par
\par
\pard\tx426 15) \b0 Marginal setulae often more than 500 \'b5m but usually less than 1000 \'b5m long, very thick-walled (4-6 \'b5m),\par
\pard        often with a multifurcate base. Ascomata 2-5 mm diam. Disc (bright) orange, lacking red shades. Spores\par
       smooth or dotted, 16.8-18.3 x 9.4-10.5 \'b5m (14.5-18 x 8-9.5, \cf1 Yao & Spooner\cf0 , 1996a). $ \b\i Cheilymenia coprinaria \i0\par
\pard\tx284\tx426\tx851 15*) \b0 Setulae less than 500 \'b5m long, with thinner (1-4 \'b5m) walls and a simple or bifurcate rooting base. Disc usually \par
\pard         reddish-orange, sometimes red or brightly orange. \b 16\b0\par
\par
\b 16) \b0 Base of marginal setulae less than 20 \'b5m wide. \lang1040 Ascomata up to 4 mm diam. \lang2057 Spores subglobose or broadly\par
       ellipsoidal (Q= 1.22), 14-16.8 x 11.5-13.6 \'b5m ( 16.5-19.5 x 12-13.5, \cf1 Moravec\cf0 , 1988).   $ \b\i Cheilymenia fraudans\par
\i0 16*) \b0 Setulae wider. Spores larger, ellipsoidal (Q= > 1.70). \b 17\par
\par
17) \b0 Ascomata up to 5 mm diam. Marginal setulae very dense. Receptacles with a brownish margin. Spores uniseriate,\par
      smooth or irregularly dotted, 16.2-19 x 9.4-11.5 \'b5m (16.5-21 x 9-11, \cf1 Moravec\cf0 , 1989). \lang1040 Asci 12-16.5\par
      \'b5m diam.   $ \b\i Cheilymenia rubra\par
\i0 17*) \b0 Ascomata < 2.5 (3) mm diam. Marginal setulae not very dense. \lang2057 Receptacles lacking a brownish margin. Spores\par
        uni- or biseriate, almost smooth, 18.5-23.2 x 10-11.4 \'b5m (21-26 x 10-13.8, \cf1 Yao & Spooner\cf0 , 1996a). \lang1040 Asci 15-18 \par
        \'b5m diam.  $ \b\i Cheilymenia fimicola\b0\i0\par
\par
\b 18) \b0 Ascomata lacking a sterile prominent margin. \lang2057 Hairs pointed, straight, rigid, dark brown. Spores with large\par
       oil drops.   (\b\i Trichophaea\b0\i0 )    \b 19\i\par
\i0 18*) \b0 Ascomata usually with a prominent margin. Hairs obtuse, hyphoid, often fasciculate, hyaline or pigmented. \par
\b         \b0 Mature spores lacking oil drops (\b\i Pseudombrophila\b0\i0 ), smooth or at most finely warted or punctate,\par
        exceptionally striate, never reticulate.    (sect. \b\i Pseudombrophila\b0\i0 )    \b 20\b0\par
\b\par
19)\b0  Marginal hairs often fasciculate, with a truncate or attenuate base. Spores narrowly ellipsoidal to (sub)fusiform,\par
\pard\li360 finely warted, 20-24.5 x 11-12 \'b5m.   $ \b\i Trichophaea gregaria\par
\pard\i0 19*) \b0 Hairs not fasciculate, with a bulbous base. Spores ellipsoidal, smooth, 15-18  x 8.5-10 \'b5m (species not  \par
\b\i         \b0\i0 described in this text).  \b\i Trichophaea subalpina\b0\i0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b\par
20) \b0 Spores more or less globose, 11.4-12.3 \'b5m diam. (10-12.5, \cf1 van Brummelen\cf0 , 1995). Receptacles laid down on a\par
       well developed  subiculum. Microsclerotia (\ldblquote bulbils\rdblquote ) present, especially in culture. \par
            $ \b\i Pseudombrophila bulbifera\b0\i0                    \b\i\par
\i0 20*) \b0 Spores ellipsoidal or cylindric-ellipsoidal to subfusiform. Subiculum\i  \i0 absent or not well developed. \b 21\par
\par
21) \b0 Mature\b  \b0 spores ornamented with parallel, oblique or transverse striae, 10.9-11.8 x 6.1-6.6 \'b5m (11-14 x 6.6-7.6,  \par
      \cf1 van Brummelen\cf0 , 1995).  $ \b\i Pseudombrophila petrakii\b0\i0  \par
\b 21*) \b0 Spores smooth or finely warted or punctate.  \b 22\par
\par
22) \b0 Intercellular pigment between apices of paraphyses absent and, consequently, hymenial surface white or very\par
       pale yellowish.    \b 23\par
22*) \b0 Intercellular pigment present. Hymenial surface pigmented (but see also remarks about \b\i P. merdaria\b0\i0 ). \b  24\par
\b0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx284\b 23\b0  Spores 15.7-16.8 x 9.4 \'b5m (14.3-18.3 x 8.7-10, \cf1 van Brummelen\cf0 , 1995), ellipsoidal (Q= 1.75). Margin of the\par
      receptacles with a collarette. $\b  \i Pseudombrophila minuta\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\i0 23*) \b0 Spores 14.7-16.1 x 7.6-8.5 \'b5m (12.3-16.6 x 6.5-8.5, \cf1 van Brummelen\cf0 , 1995), narrowly ellipsoidal  (Q= 1.90).\par
        Margin of the receptacles lacking a collarette. $ \b\i Pseudombrophila theioleuca\b0\i0  \par
\b\i\par
\i0 24) \b0 Spores 10.5-14.1 x 6-8.4 \'b5m (10.3-13.5 x 6.2-8.3, \cf1 van Brummelen\cf0 , 1995), ellipsoidal (Q= 1.67). Paraphyses\par
      usually inflated at the apices. Asci 110-137 \'b5m long. $ \b\i Pseudombrophila merdaria\par
\i0 24*) \b0 Spores more than 15 \'b5m long, narrowly ellipsoidal or subfusiform (Q \lang1040 >\lang2057  1.80). Asci larger. Paraphyses not- or\par
         hardly inflated.  \b 25\i\par
\par
