\pard\nowidctlpar\lang1040\i\par
\lang2057\b0\i0 KEY TO FIMICOLOUS \b\i SORDARIOMYCETES\b0\i0\par
(PYRENOMYCETES)\par
\pard\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b 1) \b0 Ascomata usually perithecioid, wholly or partly immersed in a stromatic tissue. Peridium made up of cells\par
     arranged in compressed rows. Apical apparatus of the asci amyloid or rarely dextrinoid. Spores dark brown, \par
     one-celled or rarely septate, usually with a germ slit. (\b\i Xylariales\b0\i0  Nannf. \b\i p.p.\b0\i0  \endash  \b\i Xylariaceae\b0\i0  Tul. & C. Tul.)               \b 2\par
1*) \b0 Ascomata perithecioid or cleistothecioid, with or without a stromatic tissue. Peridium differently structured.\par
      Asci non-amyloid. Spores hyaline or pigmented, one, two or more celled, with or without germ pore(s) or slits.    \b 8\b0                               \par
      \b\par
2) \b0 Stromata reduced, pseudoparenchymatous, sessile, slightly effuse or clypeate or annulate, more or less\par
     immersed in the substratum, containing one to several ascomata. Spores one- or two-celled, the latter with a\par
     hyaline basal apiculus and a pigmented, (sub)fusiform or ellipsoidal (equilateral) to (sub)amygdaliform\par
     (inequilateral) apical part.   (\b\i Hypocopra\b0\i0 )      \b 3\par
2*) \b0 Stromata well developed, prosenchymatous, upright, stipitate, with a fertile, more or less discoidal, flattened,\par
       whitish upper part, containing numerous ascomata. Spores one-celled, slightly to markedly inequilateral.\par
                                       (\b\i Poronia\b0\i0 )         \b 7\par
\par
3) \b0 Stromata covered with a dark tomentum. Apical apparatus of the asci dextrinoid. Spores two-celled, strongly \par
     inequilateral, 17-19 x 7.6-8.5 \'b5m.   $ \b\i Hypocopra equorum \b0\i0 f. \b\i leporina\par
\i0 3*) \b0 Stromata non-tomentose. Apical apparatus of the asci amyloid. Spores one- or two-celled, equilateral or \par
      inequilateral. \b 4\par
\par
4) \b0 Stromata reduced, annulate, pale, containing a single perithecium. Spores two-celled, inequilateral.  \b 5\par
4*) \b0 Stromata more developed, darker, usually clypeate, containing one to several perithecia. Spores equilateral  \par
      or slightly inequilateral, two-celled (but see also remarks about \b\i H. brefeldii\b0\i0 ).   \b 6\par
\par
5)\b0  Spores decidedly\b  \b0 amygdaliform,\b  \b0 26.2-33.6 x 11.5-12.6 \'b5m (23-27 x 11-13, \cf1 Krug & Cain\cf0 , 1974b). Germ slit \par
     13-25 \'b5m long.    $\b  \i Hypocopra antarctica\b0\i0  \par
\b 5*) \b0 Spores slightly inequilateral to amygdaliform, rarely equilateral and ellipsoidal, very variable in size,\par
       27.3-39.4 x 13.6-21 \'b5m. Germ slit 18-23 \'b5m long.  $ \b\i Hypocopra \b0 aff.\b  festucacea\par
\i0\par
6) \b0 Stromata containing one or occasionally a few perithecia.\b  \b0 Spores ellipsoidal to fusiform, usually equilateral, \par
     24-30.4 x 13.6-15.2 \'b5m (23-27 x 13-14, \cf1 Krug & Cain\cf0 , 1974b), with germ slit 14-17 \'b5m long. \par
                         $ \b\i Hypocopra brefeldii\b0\i0                               \par
\b 6*) \b0 Stromata containing a single perithecium. Spores ellipsoidal, often slightly inequilateral, 39-44 x 21-26 \'b5m        \par
\pard       (32-41 x 17-20, \cf1 Krug & Cain\cf0 , 1974b), with germ slit 26-29 \'b5m long.   \lang1040 $ \b\i Hypocopra merdaria\i0\par
\par
7)\b0  Disc 3-12 mm diam. Spores 20-22.8 x 8.5-10 \'b5m (Q= 1.81-2.40; mean Q= 2.24).  \lang2057 $ \b\i Poronia punctata \b0\i0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b 7*) \b0 Disc slightly smaller, 3-8 mm diam. Spores 26.2-31.5 x 14.7-15.8 \'b5m (Q= 1.51-2.22; mean Q= 1.86). \par
                                    $ \b\i Poronia erici\par
\i0\par
8) \b0 Perithecia (or rarely cleistothecia) and stromatic tissues usually vividly coloured, membranous or fleshy. Apical \par
     paraphyses (= periphysoids) present, deliquescent at maturity. Spores lacking both pores and germ slits. Asci\par
     usually 8-spored, often persistent. (\b\i Hypocreales \b0\i0 Lindau)                                \b 9\par
8*) \b0 Ascomata and stromatic tissues (the latter rarely present) typically dark, membranous or coriaceous, or\cf1\par
\cf0        perithecia with more vivid tinges, but only when (long)-beaked. Periphysoids absent. Paraphyses usually mixed\par
       with the asci. Spores with pore(s) or germ slits, exceptionally lacking both. Asci (2) 4-polyspored, persistent or \par
       deliquescent at maturity.  \b 10\par
\par
9) \b0 Ascomata comparatively pale, whitish to yellow-orange, sometimes brown, not changing colour in KOH, \par
     superficial or immersed (\b\i Bionectriaceae \b0\i0 Samuels & Rossman). Stromata present, orange-reddish outside,\par
     semi-immersed. Asci clavate. Spores one-celled, smooth, hyaline, ellipsoidal, with a gelatinous perisporium\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx284\tx426      (\b\i Selinia\b0\i0 ), 57.7-63 x 23-24 \'b5m. $ \b\i Selinia pulchra\b0\i0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b 9*) \b0 Ascomata brightly coloured, orange-reddish to vivid pink or purple, changing colour in KOH, superficial.\par
       (\b\i Nectriaceae \b0\i0 Tul. & C. Tul.). Stromata absent. Perithecia globose to subpyriform, very small. Asci narrowly\par
       clavate or cylindric. Spores one-celled or rarely one-septate, ornamented, pigmented (pale brown-yellowish), \par
       globose to ellipsoidal  (\b\i Neocosmospora\b0\i0 ). Spores rugose, 9.5-10.4 x 8.5-10.4 \'b5m, globose or broadly ellipsoidal. \par
                                                                                                                   $ \b\i Neocosmospora vasinfecta \b0\i0 var. \b\i vasinfecta\par
\par
\i0 10) \b0 Stromatic tissues absent or, when exceptionally present, building up a basal crust. Ascomata very small, often\par
      globose and hairy. Asci small, globose or ovoid, usually catenate, deliquescent at maturity, lacking an apical  \par
      ring. Paraphyses absent. Spores often dextrinoid in the early stages, hyaline or pigmented but not dark, \par
      conglobate inside the asci, usually one-celled, exceptionally with a gelatinous equipment. \par
                                                                                                    (\b\i Microascales \b0\i0 Luttrell ex Benny & Kimbr.) \b                  11\i\par
\i0 10*) \b0 Stromatic tissues sometimes present, but not forming crusts. Ascomata small to comparatively large,\par
        polymorphous, glabrous or hairy. Asci fasciculate, rarely globose or ovoid, often cylindric or claviform,\par
        with or without an apical ring. Paraphyses usually present. Spores exceptionally dextrinoid, hyaline to pigmented,\par
        up to dark brown or black, uni- biseriate to conglobate, one-celled or septate, with germ pore(s) or slits\par
        (rarely lacking both), often with a gelatinous equipment.  (\b\i Sordariales \b0\i0 Chad. ex D. Hawksw. & Erikss.)              \b 13\i\par
\par
\i0 11) \b0 Ascomata  semi-immersed, orange-yellowish, ostiolate (perithecioid), with a long beak fimbriate at the apex. Spores\par
       non-dextrinoid (\b\i Microascales incertae sedis p.p.\b0\i0 ), hyaline, elongate-allantoid, with an indistinct germ pore  \par
       (\b\i Viennotidia\b0\i0  \b\i p.p.\b0\i0 ), 5.2-7.1 x 1.5-2 \'b5m. $ \b\i Viennotidia fimicola\b0\i0  \par
\b 11*) \b0 Ascomata superficial, dark, often hairy, non-ostiolate (cleistothecioid) in the species present in Italy or ostiolate \par
        and then with or without a long beak. Spores dextrinoid, pigmented at maturity, with (one) or two germ pores.\par
                                                                                                                      (\b\i Microascaceae \b0\i0 Luttrell ex Malloch)           \b 12\i\par
\par
\i0 12) \b0 Ascomata globose, 150-250 \'b5m diam., with an intrathecal hyphal skein (\ldblquote capillitium\rdblquote ), outside with one or\par
       a few papillae, each of which supports a long tuft of hairs (\b\i Enterocarpus\b0\i0 ). \lang1036 Spores 9.5-11.5 x 6.8-9 \'b5m,\par
\lang2057        ellipsoidal-sublimoniform, often slightly asymmetrical, with two germ pores.  $ \b\i Enterocarpus grenotii\b0\i0                           \par
\b 12*)\b0  Ascomata 190-220 \'b5m diam., exceptionally subglobose, usually ellipsoidal, ovoid or subtriangular,  lacking a\par
       \ldblquote capillitium\rdblquote , with scattered hairs or tufts of long, circinate hairs placed at the angles. Spores 4.7-5.7 x 3.6-4.2 \'b5m,\par
        ellipsoidal  or sublimoniform, sometimes ovoid or subglobose, with two indistinct germ pores.\par
                                                                                                        \lang1040 (\b\i Kernia p.p.\b0\i0 )                                    $  \b\i Kernia nitida\par
\i0\par
\pard\lang2057 13) \b0 Ascomata usually superficial, perithecioid or cleistothecioid, hairy or setulose, rarely glabrous or nearly so. \par
       Peridium pseudoparenchymatous or sometimes cephalothecoid. Asci usually deliquescent in the early stages,\par
       without an apical ring. Spores one-celled, pigmented at maturity but occasionally very dark, sometimes \par
       dextrinoid, with one or two germ pores, without a gelatinous equipment. Paraphyses absent or short and \par
       ephemeral.  \b 14\par
\pard\nowidctlpar 13*) \b0 Ascomata superficial or (semi)immersed, glabrous or hairy. Peridium pseudoparenchymatous (with some \par
        exceptions). Asci almost always persistent, sometimes with an apical ring. Spores uni- to poly-celled, hyaline \par
        to dark, non-dextrinoid, often with a gelatinous equipment. Paraphyses usually present.   \b 31\par
\par
\pard 14) \b0 Ascomata more or less glabrous or with pale setulae, which are usually denser around the ostiole (when present). \par
       Peridium light. Spores comparatively large, non-dextrinoid, occasionally with one, usually with two conspicuous\par
       germ pores. Almost always mycoparasitic. (\b\i Ceratostomataceae\b0\i0  G. Winter)       \b 15\b0  \par
\b 14*) \b0 Ascomata with dark hairs or setulae, rarely glabrous. Peridium usually dark. Spores often small, rarely\par
        dextrinoid, with one or two inconspicuous germ pores. \lang1036 Habitat: on dung, vegetable debris, soil.\par
     (\b\i Chaetomiaceae \b0\i0 G. Winter)            \b 17\b0\par
\par
\b 15) \b0 Ascomata pale yellowish, subglobose to subpyriform, ostiolate, glabrous, 100-175 \'b5m diam. Asci cylindric, \par
       \lang2057 26-38 \'b5m long. Spores dark brown-grey, smooth, ovoid, 5.7-6.6 x 3.8 \'b5m, with one germ pore. \lang1036 Parasitic on \par
       \b\i Thelebolus\b0\i0 .  ( ) \ldblquote\b\i Sordaria\b0\i0\rdblquote  \b\i minima\b0\i0  \b\i s.\b0\i0  Massee & Salmon \b\i et auct. plur\b0\i0 .   \par
\lang2057\b 15*) \b0 Ascomata golden yellow,\b\i  \b0\i0 (sub)globose or broadly pyriform, ostiolate, 200-300 \'b5m diam., with hairs \par
         crowning the neck base. Asci clavate to clavate-sacciform, 45-70 \'b5m long. Spores dark brown, smooth or \par
         ornamented, ellipsoidal-sublimoniform to fusiform, with two germ pores (one at each end).   \b 16\par
\b0\par
\b 16) \b0 Spores finely pitted (\b\i Persiciospora p.p.\b0\i0 ), symmetrical, ellipsoidal-fusiform, 19-21 x 8.5-9 \'b5m. Usually parasitic \par
       on \b\i Fusarium \i0 sp\i . \b0\i0 $ \b\i Persiciospora moreaui\i0       \i                                                                                                        \b0\i0\par
\b 16*) \b0 Spores smooth (\b\i Melanospora\b0\i0 ), asymmetrical (flattened on one side), ellipsoidal-sublimoniform, 21.1-22 x \par
         10.5-11.5 \'b5m. Parasitic on various discomycetes or fimicolous.  \lang1040 $ \b\i Melanospora brevirostris\b0\i0\par
           \i\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\lang2057\b\i0 17) \b0 Ascomata ostiolate. Exoperidium of a \i textura angularis\i0 , sometimes \i intricata \i0 or \i epidermoidea\i0 , exceptionally\par
       \i cephalothecoidea \i0 or \i prismatica\i0 . Hairs often branched, warted and spirally coiled. Asci clavate or cylindric,\par
       rarely ovoid or  fusiform. Spores with one or two germ pores (one in the Italian species studied so far).   \par
                           (\b\i Chaetomium\b0\i0 )           \b 18\i\par
\i0 17*) \b0 Ascomata non-ostiolate. Exoperidium cephalothecoid. Hairs simple (occasionally branched), smooth to \par
        verrucose, flexuous or circinate at the tips. Asci clavate or ovoid. Spores with one germ pore. \par
                (\b\i Chaetomidium\b0\i0  \b\i p.p.\b0\i0 )            \b 30\par
\par
18) \b0 Spores triangular in frontal view, 8.5-9.5 x 4.7-5.7 x 3.8-4.7 \'b5m (9-12 x 5-7 x 4-5, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986).\par
\i        \i0 Peridium cephalothecoid.   $ \b\i Chaetomium trigonosporum\par
\i0 18*) \b0 Spores differently shaped. Peridium differently structured. \b 19\i\par
\par
\i0 19) \b0 Spores lenticular, subglobose in frontal view, ellipsoidal with rounded ends in side view, 7.3-7.8 x 7.3-7.5 \par
      x 4.7-5.2 \'b5m (6-7.5 x 4-5, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al\i0 , 1986), with an indistinct germ pore. Peridium of a \i textura angularis\i0 .  \par
      Hairs 2-2.5 \'b5m diam., spirally coiled and circinate at the apex. $ \b\i Chaetomium oblatum\b0\i0                      \b\i\par
\i0 19*) \b0 Spores differently shaped.   \b 20\par
\par
20) \b0 Asci clavate. Spores biseriate to conglobate. Peridium of a \i textura angularis\i0  or \i intricata\i0 , sometimes \par
       \i epidermoidea\b\i0  \b0 or \i prismatica\i0 . \b 21\i\par
\i0 20*) \b0 Asci narrowly cylindric. Spores uniseriate. Peridium of a \i textura angularis\i0 . \b 28\par
\par
\pard 21) \b0 Perithecia with a dark collar around the ostiole. Spores\b  \b0 dextrinoid in the early stages, pale grey at maturity,\par
\pard\nowidctlpar       limoniform-subglobose, biapiculate, with an apical germ pore. \b 22\par
21*) \b0 Perithecia lacking a dark collar. Immature spores non-dextrinoid, usually brown or dark grey at maturity. \b 23\b0            \par
\par
\pard\b 22) \b0 Perithecia usually ovoid or ellipsoidal. Peridium all of a \i textura angularis\i0 . Apical hairs with spirally coiled,\par
      often branched ends (branches in turn spirally coiled).  \lang1031 Spores 6.8-7.5 x 5.7-6.3 \'b5m  (5.5-7.5 x 5-6.5, \cf1 von Arx\cf0\par
      \lang2057\i et al.\i0 , 1986).   $ \b\i Chaetomium bostrychodes\par
\i0 22*) \b0 Perithecia usually ampulliform. Only the apical portion of the peridium a \i textura prismatica\i0 . Apical hairs \par
         spirally coiled, but rarely branched. Spores 6.1-6.6 x 5.2-6.1 \'b5m (5.5-7.5 x 5-6.5, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986).\par
\pard\nowidctlpar                    $ \b\i Chaetomium robustum\b0\i0                                                                                            \b\i\par
\i0\par
23)\b0  Spores with an apical germ pore. \b 24\par
23*) \b0 Spores with an eccentric (subapical or lateral) germ pore.  \b 27\par
\par
\pard 24) \b0 Peridium of a \i textura angularis\i0 , at intervals \i epidermoidea\i0 . Apical hairs spirally coiled. Spores watermelon \par
      seed-shaped, ovoid in frontal view, broadly ellipsoidal in side view, 13.1-14.7 x 11-12.6 x 8-10 \'b5m\par
      \lang1036 (12-16 x 9-11 x 7-10, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986).    \lang2057 $ \b\i Chaetomium semen-citrulli\par
\i0 24*) \b0 Apical hairs and spores differently shaped. \b 25\par
\i\par
\i0 25) \b0 Colonies\b  \b0 lacking exudates.\b  \b0 Apical hairs of two kinds: 1) seta-like and unbranched; 2) dichotomously branched.\par
       Peridium of a \i textura angularis\i0 , covered with a network of hyphae. Spores limoniform or ovoid, uni- or \par
       \lang1036 biapiculate, 5.5-5.8 x 3.8-4.2 x 3-3.3 \'b5m (6-7.5 x 4-5.5, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986). \lang2057 $ \b\i Chaetomium funicola\par
\i0 25*) \b0 Colonies often with greenish-yellow exudates. Apical hairs of one kind. Spores larger, limoniform, biapiculate.  \b 26\b0         \par
\b\par
26) \b0 Peridium usually of a \i textura epidermoidea\i0 . Apical hairs flexuous and dichotomously branched. \lang1036 Spores 11-11.4 x\par
      7.6-8.5 x 6.6-7.1 \'b5m (11-14 x 8-11 x 7-9, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986). \lang2057 $ \b\i Chaetomium elatum\par
\i0 26*) \b0 Peridium of a \i textura intricata\i0 . Apical hairs flexuous or more often spirally coiled, unbranched. \lang1036 Spores 8-10 x\par
\pard\nowidctlpar          6.6-9.6 x 5.7-7.6 \'b5m (9-12 x 8-10 x 6-8, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986).  \lang2057 $ \b\i Chaetomium globosum\b0\i0                                                                                                    \b\par
\pard\par
27) \b0 Perithecia 250-270 \'b5m diam. Peridium of a \i textura angularis\i0 . Apical hairs of two kinds:  the outer ones pale, \par
      strongly ramified, thin-walled, the middle ones darker, less ramified, with thicker walls. Spores \b\par
      \b0 ellipsoidal-narrowly limoniform (Q= 1.70), 9.5-11.5 x 5.7-6.5 \'b5m (8-12 x 5-7,\b  \cf1\b0 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986).\b\par
              \b0 $ \b\i Chaetomium cuniculorum\par
\i0 27*) \b0 Perithecia\b  \b0 180-230 \'b5m diam. Peridium with a superficial layer of \i textura intricata. \i0 Apical hairs with long \par
        spirally coiled ends. Spores ellipsoidal to subfusiform (Q= 1.87), 15.7-17.3 x 7.8-9.4 \'b5m.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar                 $ \b\i Chaetomium  fusisporum\par
\par
\i0 28) \b0 Spores\b  \b0 11-11.8 x 8-9 \'b5m (8-11 x 7-8, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986), broadly ovoid, sometimes biapiculate.\par
                   $ \b\i Chaetomium crispatum\par
\i0 28*) \b0 Spores smaller, (broadly) ovoid but uniapiculate.   \b 29\i\par
\par
\pard\i0 29) \b0 Apical hairs 5-8 \'b5m diam., long spirally coiled, even with spirally coiled branches. Spores 6.8-7.3 x 5.7-6.3 \'b5m\b\par
\b0       (7-8.5 x 6-7, \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986), broadly ovoid.  $ \b\i Chaetomium medusarum\b0\i0          \par
\b 29*) \b0 Apical hairs 4-6.5 \'b5m diam., long spirally coiled but lacking branches. \lang1036 Spores 8.9-9.5 x 7.3-7.9 \'b5m (8-9.5 x 7-8,  \par
\pard\nowidctlpar          \cf1 von Arx\cf0  \i et al.\i0 , 1986), ovoid. $\lang2057  \b\i Chaetomium mollicellum\par
\par
\pard\i0 30) \b0 Hairs coarsely verrucose, 2-4 \'b5m diam., often with end branches at right angle. Spores 19-21.5 x 11-13 \'b5m, \par
      ellipsoidal to broadly fusiform.   $ \b\i Chaetomidium  megasporum\par
\i0 30*) \b0 Hairs verruculose at most, 4-7 \'b5m diam., exceptionally branched. Spores 13.6-16.8 x 7.8-9 \'b5m, narrowly\par
        ellipsoidal or subfusiform.   $ \b\i Chaetomidium cephalothecoides\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\par
\pard\i0 31) \b0 Ascomata perithecioid, often hairy or setose. Spores one-celled, pale or dark brown, bilaterally flattened\par
       (discoidal), with a germ slit. (\b\i Coniochaetaceae \b0\i0 Malloch & Cain, \b\i p.p.\b0\i0 ; \b\i Coniochaeta\b0\i0 , \b\i p.p.\b0\i0 )     \b 32\b0\par
\b 31*) \b0 Ascomata perithecioid or cleistothecioid, glabrous, or hairy or setose. Spores uni- to poly-celled, hyaline or dark,\par
\pard\nowidctlpar          not bilaterally flattened, without a germ slit, sometimes with germ pore(s).  \b 34\par
\i\par
\pard\i0 32) \b0 Perithecia\b  \b0 sometimes with a glabrous neck, but usually with short (28-45 x 4-5 \'b5m) setae. \lang1040 Asci 75-100 x\par
       7.5-8 \'b5m. Spores 8.4-9.5 x 6.3-7.3 x 4.5-5.5 \'b5m. $ \b\i Coniochaeta leucoplaca\b0\i0\par
\b 32*) \b0 Setae longer, always present. \lang2057 Asci and spores larger.  \b 33\b0\par
\par
\b 33) \b0 Asci 136-157 x 10.5-15.7 \'b5m. Spores 13.7-15.8 x 10.5-12.6 x 6.7-9.4 \'b5m.    \lang1040 $ \b\i Coniochaeta vagans\b0\i0  \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b 33*) \b0 Asci 165-200 x 13-16 \'b5m. Spores 17.8-21 x 13.7-15.8 x 6.7-8.9 \'b5m.  $ \b\i Coniochaeta scatigena\par
\par
\i0 34) \b0 Peridial cells large, up to 30 \'b5m diam. \lang2057 Asci more or less cylindric, usually with a thickened apical ring. Spores\b  \par
\b0        uniseriate, one-celled, dark brown, with one germ pore, often with a gelatinous sheath but never with gelatinous\par
       caudae. Paraphyses swollen, not mixed with the asci.    (\b\i Sordariaceae\b0\i0  G. Winter, \b\i p.p.\b0\i0 )          \b 35\i\par
\i0 34*)\b0  Peridial cells usually smaller. Asci rarely cylindric, usually claviform to saccate, 4- to polyspored, with or\par
        without an apical ring. Spores uni- or  biseriate or conglobate, one- to poly-celled, hyaline or partly or fully\par
        pigmented at maturity, with 0-4 germ pores, with or without a gelatinous sheath or caudae. Paraphyses often\par
        filiform and mixed with the asci. (\b\i Lasiosphaeriaceae\b0\i0  Nannf.)          \b 40\par
\par
35) \b0 Ascomata cleistothecioid. Asci 2-spored, vanishing. Spores warted, without a gelatinous sheath, 10.5-14.4 x\par
       \lang1040 7.6-10.6 \'b5m.  $ \b\i Copromyces bisporus\par
\i0 35*) \b0 Ascomata perithecioid. \lang2057 Asci 8-spored, persistent. Spores smooth, often with a gelatinous sheath. (\b\i Sordaria\b0\i0 )     \b 36\par
\i\par
\i0 36) \b0 Spores subglobose or broadly ovoid, with or without a gelatinous sheath.  \b 37\par
36*) \b0 Spores narrowly to broadly ellipsoidal, with a gelatinous sheath. \b 38\par
\par
37) \b0 Spores 21.8-23.7 x 14.2-17.1 \'b5m (18-23 x 13-15, \cf1 Lundqvist\cf0 , 1972), broadly ovoid, sometimes broadly ellipsoidal\par
       (Q= 1.44), with a gelatinous sheath.  $ \b\i Sordaria lappae\par
\i0 37*) \b0 Spores 20-23 x 15-18 \'b5m (20-25 x 15.5-19, \cf1 Lundqvist\cf0 , 1972), subglobose or broadly ovoid (Q= 1.29), lacking\par
        a gelatinous sheath at least in collections isolated from carnivore dung.   \lang1040 $ \b\i Sordaria humana\b0\i0  \par
\b\par
38) \b0 Perithecia 300-340 x 250-270 \'b5m. Spores ellipsoidal, 18-23 x 10-14 \'b5m (18-24 x 11-13, \cf1 Lundqvist\cf0 , 1972). \par
                             $ \b\i Sordaria fimicola\par
\i0 38*) \b0 Perithecia and spores larger.   \lang2057\b 39\b0                                        \b\i\par
\par
\i0 39) \b0 Perithecia 450-500 x 400-450 \'b5m. Spores ellipsoidal, sometimes ovoid, 26.7-29.4 x 16.2-18.3 \'b5m (23-29 x \par
       14.5-17, \cf1 Lundqvist\cf0 , 1972).  \lang1040 $ \b\i Sordaria superba\b0\i0  \par
\b 39*) \b0 Perithecia 550-800 x 500-600 \'b5m. Spores ellipsoidal, 32.5-36 x 18.3-21 \'b5m (28-35 x 18-22, \cf1 Lundqvist\cf0 , 1972).    \par
                       \lang2057 $ \b\i Sordaria macrospora\par
\par
\i0 40) \b0 Asci 4- or 8-spored, with a thickened apical ring and often with a subapical plasma globulus. Immature spores \par
       hyaline, cylindric-vermiform, one- or two-celled, sometimes poly-septate, usually with a simple gelatinous \par
       cauda at each end and containing numerous oil drops. Spores slowly and irregularly maturing with a \par
       pigmented upper cell and hyaline pedicel. (\b\i Lasiosphaerioideae p p.\b0\i0 , after Lundqvist, 1972)      \b 41\b0    \b\par
40*) \b0 Asci 4- to polyspored, with or without an apical ring, usually lacking a plasma globulus. Spores at least partly\par
        pigmented at maturity and only in this state discharged from the asci (never when hyaline), exceptionally\par
        cylindric-vermiform, one- to four-celled, often with a gelatinous equipment in the shape of sheath or caudae,\par
        usually not containing oil drops.   (\b\i Podosporoideae\b0\i0  N. Lundq.)       \b 45\par
\par
41) \b0 Ascomata cleistothecioid (\b\i Tripterosporella\b0\i0 ), hairy. Asci 8-spored, with a subapical plasma globulus. Spore\par
